# DESIGN.md — Audience, Intent, and User Tests

## Audience
The filmmaker's family, Ethiopian young people, and viewers interested in family heritage and community values.

## Intent
By the end of the film, viewers should appreciate the father's diligence in farming, the care with which he raised his family, and his contribution to community mediation and reconciliation. Viewers should also understand why family stories and values should be passed to future generations.

## Story summary
The filmmaker's family story is rooted in North Shewa, Ethiopia. The filmmaker describes his father as a hardworking farmer and a role model in agricultural and social life. He worked hard to raise the family with love and good values. He was respected in the community for participating in customary shimgilna (mediation) and reconciliation. The family learned perseverance, diligence, love, and respect from him. The filmmaker did not supply a specific date, village, crop, named dispute, or single historical incident; none has been added.

## Visual treatment and factual boundaries
Generated visuals are illustrative reconstructions, not archival footage. Use a generic, non-identifiable father figure unless recorded informed consent permits an identifiable likeness. Do not invent a particular village, date, crop, dispute, quotation, or ceremonial detail.

