## Shot rationale
| Shot ID | Why this shot exists | Intended audience response |
|---|---|---|
| shot_01 | Establish the North Shewa setting. | Understand the family's regional roots. |
| shot_02 | Introduce agriculture as part of the father's life. | Recognize the role of farming and work. |
| shot_03 | Introduce the father through a non-identifiable illustration. | Focus on the person at the heart of the story. |
| shot_04 | Connect the father to his agricultural work. | Appreciate practical diligence. |
| shot_05 | Represent care for the family. | Feel the importance of family love. |
| shot_06 | Represent raising the family with good values. | Reflect on moral guidance and care. |
| shot_07 | Show the father's respected community role. | Understand his social contribution. |
| shot_08 | Illustrate customary mediation and reconciliation. | Appreciate community harmony and mutual respect. |
| shot_09 | Visualize perseverance through difficulty. | Recognize patience and hard work as lessons. |
| shot_10 | Close with the intergenerational legacy and AI disclosure. | Remember the message: our story is our identity. |

Do not fill user-test sections with assumed or invented feedback. Record what participants actually said and what changed as a result.
